# Shared original heuristics, scoped through explicit profile attachments.
for id,statement,why,limits in [
('hierarchy','Give the primary message the strongest visual emphasis; supporting evidence and action follow.','A viewer can find the proposition without reading every element.','Hierarchy changes for product photography and utility notifications; no fixed font-size ratio.'),
('legibility','Review copy at actual displayed size, crop and viewing distance.','Artboard resolution alone cannot establish reading ease.','No universal minimum raster font size; script, density and surface matter.'),
('spacing','Keep deliberate space between text, marks and subject; protect critical content from edges and overlays.','Separation helps grouping and prevents accidental collisions.','Do not invent a platform safe area; numeric insets require a reference canvas.'),
('message-focus','Choose message depth to match dwell time and user intent.','A small banner or moving-traffic billboard has less reading opportunity than a brochure.','No universal word budget; required qualifiers must survive.'),
('copy-image','Make visual and copy support the same truthful proposition.','Contradictory imagery can create an unsupported impression.','Catalog and responsive assets may forbid or discourage added text; brand text rules cannot override that.'),
('information-flow','Use a coherent reading sequence, language direction and sequence of cards/pages.','The offer, support and action should be understandable in order.','Cards may reorder; essential qualification must not rely on an unseen later card.'),
('exact-copy','Verify every baked word, numeral, accent and qualifier in the actual generated artwork.','Image generation can misspell or omit exact text.','OCR is a candidate check, not proof; semantic/visual review required.')]:
    rule(id,'heuristic',['editorial'],statement,rationale=why,limits=limits)
